/38/387e22e062c4ff7f24d26561fe369041f11f59a2b0305f8dc7b3ce49d411031a.png)\n\n**Step 2**: Compute the Jacobian determinant corresponding to ${T}^{-1}:$\n\nThe Jacobian determinant corresponding to ${T}^{-1}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(u,v)}{∂(x,y)} & =\\left|\\begin{matrix}\\frac{∂u}{∂x}&\\frac{∂u}{∂y}\\\\\\frac{∂v}{∂x}&\\frac{∂v}{∂y}\\end{matrix}\\right| \\\\ &=\\left|\\begin{matrix}1&-1\\\\0&1\\end{matrix}\\right| \\\\ &=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 3**: Compute the Jacobian determinant corresponding to $T:$\n\nThe Jacobian determinant corresponding to $T$ is\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}={(\\frac{∂(u,v)}{∂(x,y)})}^{-1}=(1)^{-1}=1.\n$$\n\nNote that $\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}\\ne 0$ everywhere inside $Δ.$  In other words, $T$ has no critical points inside $Δ.$\n\n**Step 4**: Compute the required area.\n\nWe calculate the required area by performing the change of variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\iint_D dxdy &=\\iint_Δ |\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}|\\,dudv \\\\ &=\\iint_Δ |1|\\,dudv \\\\ &=1\\int_{-4}^{4}[\\int_{u^{2}}^{16}dv]du \\\\ &=1\\int_{-4}^{4}[v]_{u^{2}}^{16}du \\\\ &=1\\int_{-4}^{4}(16)-(u^{2})du \\\\ &=1\\int_{-4}^{4}(16 - u^{2})du \\\\ &=1[- \\frac{u^{3}}{3} + 16 u]_{-4}^{4} \\\\ &=1(((64)+(- \\frac{64}{3}))-((-64)+(\\frac{64}{3}))) \\\\ &=1(\\frac{256}{3}) \\\\ &=\\frac{256}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139536028 17592186045443 true] [17592186558896 1080 "- \\frac{256}{3}" 13194139536028 17592186045443 true] [17592186558896 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139536028 17592186045443 true] [17592186558896 1083 #uuid "b27db125-1811-506c-a9a7-73bd26f5a681" 13194139536028 17592186045443 true] [17592186558897 1075 #edb/ref 17592186558857 13194139536028 17592186045443 true] [17592186558897 1075 #edb/ref 17592186558859 13194139536028 17592186045443 true] [17592186558897 1075 #edb/ref 17592186558882 13194139536028 17592186045443 true] [17592186558897 1075 #edb/ref 17592186558903 13194139536028 17592186045443 true] [17592186558897 1075 #edb/ref 17592186558915 13194