 Compute the Jacobian determinant corresponding to ${T}^{-1}:$\n\nThe Jacobian determinant corresponding to ${T}^{-1}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(u,v)}{∂(x,y)} & =\\left|\\begin{matrix}\\frac{∂u}{∂x}&\\frac{∂u}{∂y}\\\\\\frac{∂v}{∂x}&\\frac{∂v}{∂y}\\end{matrix}\\right| \\\\ &=\\left|\\begin{matrix}5&-2\\\\1&1\\end{matrix}\\right| \\\\ &=7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 3**: Compute the Jacobian determinant corresponding to $T:$\n\nThe Jacobian determinant corresponding to $T$ is\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}={(\\frac{∂(u,v)}{∂(x,y)})}^{-1}=(7)^{-1}=\\frac{1}{7}.\n$$\n\nNote that $\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}\\ne 0$ everywhere inside $Δ.$  In other words, $T$ has no critical points inside $Δ.$\n\n**Step 4**: Compute the required area.\n\nWe calculate the required area by performing the change of variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\iint_D dxdy &=\\iint_Δ |\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}|\\,dudv \\\\ &=\\iint_Δ |\\frac{1}{7}|\\,dudv \\\\ &=\\frac{1}{7}\\int_{-1}^{1}[\\int_{u^{2}}^{1}dv]du \\\\ &=\\frac{1}{7}\\int_{-1}^{1}[v]_{u^{2}}^{1}du \\\\ &=\\frac{1}{7}\\int_{-1}^{1}(1)-(u^{2})du \\\\ &=\\frac{1}{7}\\int_{-1}^{1}(1 - u^{2})du \\\\ &=\\frac{1}{7}[- \\frac{u^{3}}{3} + u]_{-1}^{1} \\\\ &=\\frac{1}{7}(((1)+(- \\frac{1}{3}))-((-1)+(\\frac{1}{3}))) \\\\ &=\\frac{1}{7}(\\frac{4}{3}) \\\\ &=\\frac{4}{21}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139536028 17592186045443 true] [17592186558905 1080 "\\frac{128}{3}" 13194139536028 17592186045443 true] [17592186558905 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139536028 17592186045443 true] [17592186558905 1083 #uuid "c881d35c-8be6-578a-ac79-fe3e965182f7" 13194139536028 17592186045443 true] [17592186558906 1080 "\\frac{2}{7}" 13194139536028 17592186045443 true] [17592186558906 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139536028 17592186045443 true] [17592186558906 1083 #uuid "ca8ec194-90f6-583a-9a4b-6db556579326" 13194139536028 17592186045443 true] [17592186558907 1075 #edb/ref 17592186558877 13194139536028 17592186045443 true] [17592186558907 1075 #edb/ref 1759218655888